{"qid":"Q402580","names":["Mataram Kingdom"],"title":"Mataram Kingdom","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Mataram Kingdom was a Hindu-Buddhist Javanese polity that flourished between roughly the eighth and eleventh centuries, founded by King Sanjaya of the Wangsa Sanjaya line and later sharing power with the Shailendra dynasty, who built the Borobudur stupa complex (c. 800–825 CE) and Prambanan temple compound (c. 850 CE). In its Sanjaya phase the kingdom controlled fertile Central Javanese agricultural hinterlands and commanded significant corvée labour for monument construction. Following a disputed succession and possibly a volcanic eruption of Mount Merapi, the court relocated to East Java in the early tenth century under King Mpu Sindok (r. c. 929–947), where the dynasty reorganised and later gave rise to the Kediri and Singhasari kingdoms. The terminal date of 1010 marks the defeat of the last Mataram-descended ruler Dharmawangsa Teguh by the Srivijayan-backed Wurawari coalition.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Mataram's territorial extent is reconstructed from epigraphy and temple locations; its frontiers, especially in the interior of Java and towards coastal ports, are not directly attested and vary significantly across scholarly reconstructions.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Mataram Kingdom","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mataram_Kingdom"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Borobudur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Prambanan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prambanan"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Mataram Kingdom","rulers":[{"q